# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Jinzhe Zeng et al. (2025). DeePMD-kit v3: A Multiple-Backend Framework for Machine Learning Potentials.
#   Journal of Chemical Theory and Computation. doi:10.1021/acs.jctc.5c00340  arXiv:2502.19161v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2502.19161v2 (sha256 fd3eb31855e11fe3...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 403 (Software/implementation). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/zeng2025deepmd.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the software paper's benchmark: water models DPA-1
# without attention (L=0; also compressed), DPA-1 with two attention
# layers (L=2) and DPA-2 (medium), all with 6 A cutoffs and 240-240-240
# fitting nets, timed in LAMMPS MD on water systems of 192 to 98,304
# atoms in FP64 and FP32 with each backend. The H100 timings (Table S1)
# are encoded; the A800 and RTX 4090 tables (S2, S3) are summarised in
# gaps. No accuracy metrics are reported; the training data of the water
# models are not described.

